description: TypeScript backend conventions for Twitch, the event bus, and Fastify
globs: src/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Backend

- ESM + Node 20. Imports use `.js` specifiers (`../events.js`).
- Extend `AppEvent` in `src/events.ts` before emitting a new type. Names are dotted (`chat.message`, `channel.subscription`).
- Subscribe to Twitch only in `src/twitch/eventsub.ts`. Resolve emotes/badges before emit so overlays stay dumb.
- Twurple **8**: `provider.on(provider.onRefresh, handler)` and `listener.on(listener.onUserSocketConnect, handler)`.
- Auth stays in `src/twitch/auth.ts`. Tokens go to `data/tokens.json`, not the client.
- Fastify: register `/health`, `/ws`, `/oauth`, `/api/*` **before** `@fastify/static`. `/health`, `/overlays/*`, `/ws`, and `/oauth/callback` stay public. `/oauth` requires sign-in when app login is enabled. Rate-limit `/api/login`.
- App sessions persist in `data/sessions.json` keyed by `sha256(token)`, not the raw cookie. Do not keep them only in memory.
- Keep secrets in env. Do not log access or refresh tokens, or `Cookie` headers.

```ts
// BAD
listener.onUserSocketConnect((id) => { ... })

// GOOD (Twurple 8 EventEmitter)
listener.on(listener.onUserSocketConnect, (id) => { ... })
```
